{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## ADR 0058 is violated 5 times on `origin/main` today — shape 3 has live targets\n\nMeasured against `origin/main` (`e1c9eb09fa3a`) from an origin/main-based worktree, not the\nmain checkout. **That distinction mattered:** `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` sits detached at\n`2e28d817a7e`, a tree with 3908 files to origin/main's 3784, and a first scan run there\nreported 2 extra violations (`test_signing_module_split.py`, `test_agent_call_seam.py`) that do\nnot exist on `origin/main`. Any scan for this ticket must run from a worktree, not the main\ncheckout.\n\nADR 0058 decides: \"`.github/module-size-limit.txt` is the single authoritative LOC ceiling...\nNo other test may assert an upper LOC bound on a `src/rebar` file, and none may hard-code a\nceiling value.\" Every assertion below breaks **both** halves — it bounds a `src/rebar` file\n*and* hard-codes the number.\n\n| Test | Target | Assertion |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/test_run_span.py:114` | `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` | `<= 800` |\n| `tests/unit/test_header_delivery.py:302` | `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` | `<= 800` |\n| `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:394` | `src/rebar/reconciler/get_rotation.py` | `100 <= ... <= 500` |\n| `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:395` | `src/rebar/reconciler/binding_store.py` | `<= 800` |\n| `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:396` | `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_differ.py` | `<= 800` |\n\n`RECONCILER_DIR` resolves to `src/rebar/reconciler` at `:96`, so all 3 of those target\n`src/rebar`.\n\n**Both failure modes ADR 0058 predicted are present.** The 3 bare `800` literals are the\ngovernance inversion: the real cap is administrator-locked in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`,\nwhile these copies are integers any contributor can edit, and an administrator raising the cap\nwould make 3 tests fail for files that are legitimately inside the new limit. The `<= 500` on\n`get_rotation.py` is the mid-refactor failure: a multi-commit decomposition passes through\nstates where the file has grown before it shrinks.\n\n**The exemptions hold as described.** The `100 <=` lower bound at `:394` is the retained\nanti-fragmentation floor and is not a violation. `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` is\nthe sanctioned mirror — `test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap` obtains its cap from\n`read_limit()` reading `.github/module-size-limit.txt` (`:34`) and hard-codes nothing, so it\nasserts an upper bound by design and must never be flagged.\n\n**Consequence.** Shape 3 is not hypothetical: enforcement has 5 present-day targets, which also\nmeans this ticket's work now has a concrete before/after. It also refutes the \"nothing has\nreintroduced a violation, so leave ADR 0058 unenforced\" disposition — violations exist and\nwere added after the ADR.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793712582148086373,"uuid":"2e7b21c9-a02a-4674-a7e0-6a1f589e351e"}